  i Convex caches the result of a query and reuses it until the data the query reads changes, so the time in a cached result can be outdated. Reading the time can also make Convex discard cached results more often than needed.
  
  i Pass the time to the query as an argument, rounded to a coarse unit such as a minute, or have a mutation or a scheduled function store time-based state in the database.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

